 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to apply the Gaussian filter on the grayscale image. Here's how you can modify your code:
```matlab
% Read input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 0.5); % Set standard deviation as per requirement
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operator in x direction
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
% Define Sobel operator in y direction
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image and edge image
figure;
subplot(1, 2, 1);
imshow(input_image); title('Original Image');
subplot(1, 2, 2);
imshow(edge_image); title('Edge Image');
```
In this modified code, we added a new line where we define a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function. We set the size of the filter kernel as 3x3 and the standard deviation as 0.5. The `imfilter` function is then used to apply the filter to the grayscale image. The rest of the code remains the same as your initial attempt. This modification will help reduce the noise in the image before applying the Sobel edge detection algorithm.

